;; THE CANONICAL CONFIG STRUCTURE — the roots the config tree is built from.
;;
;; ⚠️ THIS IS THE STRUCTURE DEFINITION, NOT A SEED. It declares WHAT KINDS of
;; config node may exist. It carries no config VALUES, no tenant, and no corpus.
;; A separate importable seed — actual values, a demo tenant, a corpus — is a
;; different and much larger artefact. If you are looking for something to
;; populate a fresh database with, this is not it, and conflating the two is how
;; a third copy of the roots arrives.
;;
;; WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `digdir.config.db/config-roots` and
;; `digdir.config.api-keys/valid-config-roots` were two private, independent,
;; hand-written definitions of this set. They were identical, and they agreed by
;; coincidence — nothing made them agree. Both now derive from here through
;; `digdir.config.structure`, so agreement is structural rather than asserted.
;;
;; PROVENANCE — this was measured, not authored:
;;   extracted 2026-09-01 from a COPY of the live store at
;;   release-verify/server/local-db/dh_release_verify_v1 (inode 320431123),
;;   copied rather than opened because opening a datahike store can write lock
;;   and index files.
;;
;;   :config.node/root    :dataset 9   :platform 4   :runtime 5     = 18 of 18 nodes
;;   :config-def/root     :dataset 32  :platform 41  :runtime 48    = 121 of 121 definitions
;;
;;   THE SUMS ARE THE EVIDENCE, not the distinct values. A distinct query
;;   returning three is equally consistent with three roots existing, a fourth
;;   living on rows the query did not reach, and rows carrying no root at all.
;;   9+4+5=18 and 32+41+48=121 exclude all three at once — every node and every
;;   definition carries one of these, and nothing carries anything else.
;;
;;   WHAT THAT DOES NOT ESTABLISH: this is one database from one worktree. It
;;   shows the code and that tree agree. It does not show a fourth root can never
;;   appear — and #436, where a fresh database cannot serve a login because no
;;   setup path creates `__global__/:platform`, is evidence that the interesting
;;   failures are about what is ABSENT rather than what is extra.
{:roots [:platform :runtime :dataset]}
